  "solution": [
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "### Solution Strategy",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "markdownBox",
      "title": "Key Idea: The Chain Rule",
      "content": "The chain rule says that if $u(x)$ and $v(x)$ are differentiable, then their composition $u(v(x))$ can be differentiated by the following formula:\n\n$$[u(v(x))]' = u'(v(x))v'(x)$$",
      "theme": "idea"
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "**1. Identify the Layers:**",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "The outer function is $u(x) = \\sqrt{x}$ and the inner function is $v(x) = {inner_f}$.",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "**2. Outside Derivative:**",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Find $u'(v(x))$, which is $\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{v(x)}}$.",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "**3. Inside Derivative:**",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Find $v'(x)$, which is ${deriv_inner}$.",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "**4. Combine:**",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "content": "Multiply them together to get the final result:",
      "isVertical": true
    },
    {
      "type": "mathLatex",
      "content": "f'(x) = {final_ans}",
      "isDisplayMode": true
    }
